\begin_layout Standard
In the field of RL, AI approaches must be considered as black boxes, which
 is why they cannot be trusted.
 To restore this trust there is the XAI area, which tries to explain the
 black box to humans.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In order to get an explanation as simple as possible, in this thesis a human-dev
eloped heuristic is used as a reference for further explanations.
 Using heuristics developed by experts as a reference point for explanations
 is called familiarity.
 With the help of GP the finding of differences is automated and represented
 as a change in the heuristic.
 The expert still recognizes his own code and can weigh the extent of the
 change in combination with its improvement.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The extent of the changes is calculated with the help of the tree edit distance.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Motivation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Thanks to enormous progress in the field of artificial intelligence, more
 and more problems can be taken over by machines.
 In the meantime it is not only possible to relieve humans of complex tasks
 but also to develop completely new solutions to problems.
 Learning a strategy to solve a problem without prior knowledge is adressed
 in the field of reinforcement learning (RL), where an agent has to maximise
 the expected reward in an environment.
 The environment represents a Markov decision process, which is a stochastic
 form of determinism so that in each state, when performing an action, the
 same subsequent state is reached with a certail probability.
 The agent has only limited computing power at his disposal, which is why
 he must carefully weigh up exploration and exploitation in order to efficiently
 develop a strategy.
\end_layout

