\begin_layout Standard
GP offers many expansion possibilities.
 For example, fuzzy GP policies can be searched for, where even complex
 policies with many rules can be searched for without the search space becoming
 so uncontrollably large that solutions can no longer be found.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "hein_fuzzy_gp"
literal "true"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Post-hoc explanation 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Online-offline_regression"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
GP can also be used to search for interpretable post-hoc formulas that represent
 the behaviour of a black box.
 For this purpose, the blackbox-policy creates a data set with transition
 samples on the real benchmark (online learning) on which a symbolic regression
 with GP is performed.
 As Hein has found out in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
after "p. 125"
key "daniel_hein_doktorarbeit"
literal "true"

\end_inset

, policies that have been trained on offline data generated by a neuropolicy
 are almost always significantly worse than both the neuropolicy and gp
 solutions that were trained on real system dynamics.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Post-hoc statements, especially through offline learning are loss-making.
 However, surrogate models cannot only be evaluated cost-effectively and
 in parallel, but especially with autopilots or industrial controllers,
 the risk of gross misexploration is reduced, which could destroy the benchmark.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Interpretability is not sufficient - Relatability / Comprehension / weighted
 complexity
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Interpretability is so difficult to achieve in the field of AI that readable
 approaches already seem to meet all standards.
 The interpretability is often evaluated by the count of parameters and
 operators and partly additionally by the complexity of interpretation of
 the operators.
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
A popular operator weighting is used in the commercial GP tool DEAP.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
after "p.119"
key "daniel_hein_doktorarbeit"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\end_inset

 Also encapsulation of a problem or pattern matching would be properties,
 which could describe the general need of properties which a formula needs
 to have to be explainable.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
All these factors are quite good indicators, but they cannot describe the
 effort of a person to understand an approach.
 
\end_layout

