\begin_layout Subsection
STGP
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Strongly Typed Genetic Programming (STGP) is another extension of GP, where
 an explicit transformation of truth values into numbers and vice versa
 is required 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Strongly_typed_GP"
literal "true"

\end_inset

.
 In many programming languages this is done automatically, but it is very
 confusing in mathematical expressions.
 A frequent change between data types is not desired anyways.
 Values must be converted explicitly, either by if-statements or comparison
 operators.
 This property can prevent closure in certain constellations, which is why
 this possibility is checked and a mutual exclusive crossover was implemented,
 which always finds two matching nodes in trees.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Reduced operator set
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Many operators can be replaced within their function with sibling operators.
 Conceivable would be to see the operators only as representatives of their
 family or to implement associative and commutative operators as combined
 operators.
 These approaches seem to be very promising, but were not done for the sake
 of simplicity.
\end_layout

