\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Histograms for the deviation from the target action for the Mountain car
 (left) and the Industrial benchmark (right).
 In both cases the best regular GP candidate, calculated with the MSE, was
 chosen.
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The PSONN policy that was used as the black box for the IB is already too
 different at the beginning of each expert policy tested to allow for any
 hope of improvement.
 Knowledge about the strategy that PSONN was pursuing could therefore not
 be gained - at best, it is a very complex approach that can hardly be represent
ed by simple formulas.
 All GP races were too similar in their real fitness and safety to allow
 conclusions and fell far short of results trained on the real benchmark.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Normal GP results had no real advantages over the familiar results despite
 their enhanced capabilities.
 The explanatory candidates were thus able to find the result even with
 the implicitly reduced solution space, which is at least a partial success
 for trust-based GP.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Conclusion
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this thesis, familiarity was presented as an essential factor for creating
 interpretable policies.
 The implementation with the edit-distance between programming trees leads
 to results, which are structurally different from the classical GP, because
 parts of the expert policy were recognizable in the solutions.
 Schwierig waren nur sehr kleine Programme, beispielsweise Only with simple
 expert solutions (3-6 nodes) the TED lost its effect quickly, because the
 difference to the regular distance became too small.
 Therefore fixed nodes in GP-trees were introduced as a solution, which
 must not be changed.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
More extensive extensions could focus even further on human thought patterns
 in the search.
 This could be the use of if statements to further subdivide problems, weighting
 of functions or an interpretable evaluation of edits.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Reliable statements or implications about robustness and real rewards cannot
 be made due to the small number of benchmarks tested.
 However, the experiments suggest that the regression error did not differ
 significantly from solutions of classical GP, which may be due to a general
 convergence of the regression error up to the outliers.
 The real rewards of the mountain car were not only very robust against
 misruns but often even exceeded the target solution.
 In order to obtain particularly secure solutions, there are also possibilities
 for expansion here, which, for example, evaluate the candidates additionally
 based on their deviation from the start policy.
\end_layout

